Category: transitive-include. Catch2 uses names whose headers it does not include, which
libstdc++ and libc++ declare through other headers:
std::abort (<cstdlib>) after <memory>/<sstream>/<string>; errno (<cerrno>) after
<cstdlib>/<iomanip>; isspace/isdigit in the global namespace (<cctype>) after <ostream>/<stack>;
std::equal (<algorithm>) after <vector>; std::ostream (<iosfwd>) after <string>. Adds the
includes.

